WEBVTT

00:21.772 --> 00:23.482
What's he doing?

00:25.901 --> 00:28.695
Escher! Saria!

00:29.905 --> 00:32.573
Oh, Escher's singing
truly is sublime!

00:32.574 --> 00:35.284
And when accompanied
with Saria's playing...

00:35.285 --> 00:36.703
Genuinely godlike!

00:38.830 --> 00:40.331
I can't take it!

00:40.332 --> 00:41.541
Maybe I should descend?

00:41.542 --> 00:44.253
I'll descend, join the
party, and then who knows—

00:46.338 --> 00:47.088
(Splat)

00:47.089 --> 00:52.052
What fool dares throw feces-shaped
lumps of cloud matter at me?!

00:55.848 --> 00:57.974
A h-h-human?!

00:57.975 --> 01:00.602
Impossible! What could
one be doing in Paradise?!

01:02.479 --> 01:06.607
Know your place, human.
I am the angel, Jihriel.

01:06.608 --> 01:11.946
Acolyte to the 64 deities of
Paradise, a sacred envoy!

01:11.947 --> 01:14.240
Trying to act fancy
all of a sudden, huh?

01:14.241 --> 01:17.243
How are the two of you
here in the first place?

01:17.244 --> 01:19.662
This is a separate realm
from the human world.

01:19.663 --> 01:22.583
Even if you intended to come here, the
wall of realms should have kept you out!

01:23.750 --> 01:27.504
I dunno. Now, can you
teach me divine sorcery?

01:29.506 --> 01:30.882
What's the matter, child?

01:30.883 --> 01:35.887
Has the sight of my beatifically gorgeous
visage fried your puny mortal brain?

01:35.888 --> 01:38.347
I'd be open to letting you
kiss my feet, you know.

01:38.348 --> 01:39.891
Go on and kneel down.

01:39.892 --> 01:42.518
Just spill the beans
already, you angelic ass!

01:42.519 --> 01:45.688
Unless you want us to tell everybody
back home about how the servants

01:45.689 --> 01:48.065
of the divine creep on girls
while panting like a perv!

01:48.066 --> 01:52.361
Hey, stupid! No one would
believe a word you'd say!

01:52.362 --> 01:56.866
While it is true that I am capable
of bestowing divine sorcery,

01:56.867 --> 01:59.577
that is a gift reserved
for those I deem worthy.

01:59.578 --> 02:02.080
Return home now and I
won't judge you for your sins.

02:02.873 --> 02:05.918
Hurry on back. I
won't tell you again.

02:06.210 --> 02:07.960
Come on, work with me here.

02:07.961 --> 02:09.213
Luxa.

02:17.054 --> 02:19.598
I already said I
wouldn't tell you again.

02:26.522 --> 02:27.814
Well, now.

02:28.732 --> 02:31.652
You're no mere
lost lamb, are you?

02:42.955 --> 02:47.793
(I Was Reincarnated as the 7th Prince so I Can Take
My Time Perfecting My Magical Ability 2nd Season)

04:04.536 --> 04:06.746
(Episode 14: Jihriel's Miracles)

04:06.747 --> 04:09.498
What now?! Lloyd flew off somewhere!
(Episode 14: Jihriel's Miracles)

04:09.499 --> 04:10.750
What now?! Lloyd
flew off somewhere!

04:10.751 --> 04:15.129
Calm down, Ren. Did he
say anything before leaving?

04:15.130 --> 04:18.634
Um... Something
about sensing a gaze.

04:18.967 --> 04:22.679
A gaze? That
wasn't what I noticed.

04:24.473 --> 04:26.140
Sorry, I need to
step out for a bit.

04:26.141 --> 04:28.267
You too, Babylon?!

04:28.268 --> 04:29.143
Everyone is running
off on their own!

04:29.144 --> 04:31.145
Something stinks. Everyone
is running off on their own!

04:31.146 --> 04:32.564
Everyone is running
off on their own!

04:35.776 --> 04:37.945
Here's hoping those
aren't rain clouds.

04:50.791 --> 04:52.334
This is fascinating!

04:52.668 --> 04:54.837
Divine sorcery...

04:56.880 --> 04:58.131
They look just like feathers,

04:59.007 --> 05:01.134
but they're as heavy
and hard as steel!

05:02.094 --> 05:03.887
As for absorbing
it with Spelltaker...

05:04.638 --> 05:06.389
I'm not getting anything!

05:06.390 --> 05:10.643
I see. The swords, once conjured,
must count as physical objects,

05:10.644 --> 05:13.438
and not spells that
the sword can steal!

05:18.026 --> 05:24.533
I'd wager these Luxal swords he's using are
generated limitlessly just by using mana.

05:24.783 --> 05:27.035
What an amazing spell!

05:27.327 --> 05:28.704
I have to see...

05:30.289 --> 05:32.541
how durable it is!

05:33.000 --> 05:36.545
Aerolanse Zephyr Aqulanse Cascadia
Pyrlanse Incinis Terralanse Lithis.

05:48.015 --> 05:50.892
Cracks in the wall of realms?!

05:50.893 --> 05:53.145
Whoa. What're you dodging for?

05:54.980 --> 05:56.899
My Luxa is invincible!

05:58.150 --> 06:02.653
But I refuse to let it be defiled by
coming in contact with your base sorcery!

06:02.654 --> 06:04.906
And that is why I dodged.
And the only reason why!

06:04.907 --> 06:06.658
Wait, what? Huh? Hu-hu-huh?!

06:06.992 --> 06:09.161
So, he's fled.

06:10.329 --> 06:11.663
Good grief.

06:11.914 --> 06:14.666
Then how am I supposed to
experiment with its resilience?

06:15.709 --> 06:19.670
An experiment?! You
fool! Don't make me laugh!

06:19.671 --> 06:22.673
Your attacks will never
come in contact with me.

06:22.674 --> 06:25.218
I will dodge them all, and then—

06:25.219 --> 06:29.139
Dodging again? I'm afraid
you don't have that option.

06:30.933 --> 06:32.184
Shadow Wolf...

06:38.690 --> 06:39.942
Strike. (Strike)

06:50.786 --> 06:52.204
What just—

06:54.581 --> 06:58.168
And he still dodges.
I messed up.

06:59.044 --> 07:01.588
Did I misjudge the distance
for the teleportation?

07:01.922 --> 07:04.591
Shadow Wolf... Strike?!

07:05.133 --> 07:08.219
The same move Guisarme used
to such effect against Prince Lloyd...

07:08.220 --> 07:11.056
Sending matter
directly into a target.

07:11.473 --> 07:13.767
Offensive teleportation!

07:14.351 --> 07:19.355
But when used by Prince Lloyd, it's
way more powerful and more versatile!

07:19.356 --> 07:19.647
Next time I'll need to reduce
the distance as much as possible.

07:19.648 --> 07:25.027
That's a pretty impressive move, boss, but it's also a little... extreme,
maybe? Next time I'll need to reduce the distance as much as possible.

07:25.028 --> 07:25.361
I get the feeling even this dude would die, and that's kind of harsh.
Next time I'll need to reduce the distance as much as possible.

07:25.362 --> 07:27.822
Otherwise it gives him enough leeway to... I get the
feeling even this dude would die, and that's kind of harsh.

07:27.823 --> 07:29.365
I get the feeling even this dude
would die, and that's kind of harsh.

07:29.366 --> 07:34.620
Don't be silly, Grim! He
said his Luxa is invincible!

07:34.621 --> 07:36.914
There's no way this
is enough to break it!

07:36.915 --> 07:40.252
I think he might've just
been talking big, though.

07:40.711 --> 07:42.378
Either way, you can relax.

07:42.379 --> 07:46.717
I'm not going to use it quite
the way you're picturing.

07:49.344 --> 07:53.015
I wouldn't misuse
Jade's power like that.

08:05.402 --> 08:05.526
Jihriel! Prince Lloyd
doesn't intend on killing you!

08:05.527 --> 08:09.363
(Hmm...) (WHIRR) Jihriel! Prince
Lloyd doesn't intend on killing you!

08:09.364 --> 08:13.284
Quit showboating, apologize, and teach
him divine sorcery! (Hmm...) (WHIRR)

08:13.285 --> 08:14.952
My Luxa is invincible!

08:14.953 --> 08:18.289
But your magic isn't
worthy of using it to defend!

08:18.290 --> 08:22.460
Look how easily I evade you! Your
cheap party tricks are nothing to me!

08:22.461 --> 08:22.585
(Hrm...) Look how easily I evade you!
Your cheap party tricks are nothing to me!

08:22.586 --> 08:24.296
(Hrm...)

08:24.505 --> 08:28.674
It's true that, for as sure-fire as this
approach looks, it leaves a lot of openings.

08:28.675 --> 08:32.053
Stop thinking of it in
terms of the relative space

08:32.054 --> 08:34.556
between the teleported
mana signature and the target...

08:35.015 --> 08:37.809
But the relative time between
the activation of the spell and...

08:38.769 --> 08:39.978
The teleportation.

08:43.482 --> 08:45.858
It doesn't matter
how close I aim;

08:45.859 --> 08:50.030
the manifestation of the spell
gives him enough time to evade.

08:51.573 --> 08:54.409
I've seen through
your cheap tricks!

08:57.454 --> 08:58.412
It's really hard to hit a
moving target with this.

08:58.413 --> 09:00.207
Prince Lloyd! It's really hard
to hit a moving target with this.

09:00.415 --> 09:03.209
Teleporting the spell before it
activates won't be fast enough.

09:03.210 --> 09:05.837
Ideally, I send it the
moment it comes into effect.

09:05.838 --> 09:11.217
Let's try holding onto the spell until
the last second, like timing a fuse...

09:11.218 --> 09:14.595
Here he comes! Prince Lloyd!

09:14.596 --> 09:17.849
I'll have your head,
demon spawn!

09:17.850 --> 09:18.809
Now.

09:21.395 --> 09:21.602
Bwuh?!

09:21.603 --> 09:22.354
(Bwuh?!) Bwuh?!

09:26.608 --> 09:30.821
How is he casting so quickly?!
This is nothing like before!

09:31.071 --> 09:34.950
Jihriel! Just apologize already!

09:35.284 --> 09:37.494
Don't be absurd!

09:38.704 --> 09:41.998
It may be shattered,
but my Luxa is infinite!

09:41.999 --> 09:44.167
And can be repaired as
many times as need be!

09:44.168 --> 09:45.126
Infinite?!

09:45.127 --> 09:47.712
Aw, damn it, I
tried to warn you!

09:47.713 --> 09:49.589
Luxa seems like such
an incredible spell!

09:49.590 --> 09:52.217
I wonder how much it
can infinitely regenerate.

09:52.593 --> 09:53.802
I have to know!

09:54.219 --> 09:56.722
I mean, it's not all that.

09:57.097 --> 10:01.475
Y'know, I'll do you the immense
favor of letting you return safely today!

10:01.476 --> 10:05.772
Why, I'll even give you an
autograph and let you kiss my feet...

10:08.483 --> 10:10.860
It was a lie! I lied! I'm sorry!

10:10.861 --> 10:12.279
It's actually finite!

10:17.284 --> 10:17.783
(Fade...)

10:17.784 --> 10:18.159
He's looking kinda
transparent. (Fade...)

10:18.160 --> 10:20.162
He's looking kinda transparent.

10:20.662 --> 10:26.292
Well, ethereal entities like us
are basically comprised of mana.

10:26.293 --> 10:29.129
So, Luxa is neither
invincible nor infinite.

10:29.546 --> 10:33.341
It's a expenditure of mana
to manifest steel armaments.

10:33.342 --> 10:37.846
But that means as long as you have
mana, you can keep making more!

10:38.764 --> 10:41.015
Well fought, child.

10:41.016 --> 10:45.311
But you have lost your
chance to learn divine sorcery.

10:45.312 --> 10:48.105
You can live the rest of your life
wondering "what is divine sorcery?"

10:48.106 --> 10:49.732
(Stupid! Jerk!) You can live the rest of
your life wondering "what is divine sorcery?"

10:49.733 --> 10:50.567
You can live the rest of your life
wondering "what is divine sorcery?"

10:50.692 --> 10:52.026
Hmph! (Bzzzzzzzz)
(Wahbahbahbahbah)

10:52.027 --> 10:53.320
(Bzzzzzzzz) (Wahbahbahbahbah)

10:53.654 --> 10:55.404
Wh-What are you doing, child?

10:55.405 --> 10:57.657
Just sharing some
of my mana with you.

10:57.658 --> 10:59.575
That should have
you feeling better.

10:59.576 --> 11:02.703
But I tried to kill you...

11:02.704 --> 11:07.459
Doesn't matter! I just
want to learn divine sorcery.

11:11.213 --> 11:12.630
Your name is...
Lloyd, then, child?

11:12.631 --> 11:13.214
(Burp...) Your name
is... Lloyd, then, child?

11:13.215 --> 11:15.132
Your name is...
Lloyd, then, child?

11:15.133 --> 11:16.384
He's looking kinda chonky.

11:16.385 --> 11:18.219
You gave him too much mana.

11:18.220 --> 11:18.761
Immense mana
unbecoming of mankind,

11:18.762 --> 11:20.596
You want some too, Grim? Immense
mana unbecoming of mankind,

11:20.597 --> 11:21.013
Immense mana
unbecoming of mankind,

11:21.014 --> 11:23.308
wielded by an innocent child...

11:24.184 --> 11:25.476
I know what this is...

11:25.477 --> 11:26.143
(Wahbahbahbah)

11:26.144 --> 11:27.645
Very well. (Wahbahbahbah)

11:27.646 --> 11:27.979
(Wahbahbahbah)

11:27.980 --> 11:31.108
I shall bestow divine
sorcery upon you.

11:31.567 --> 11:34.486
It's a chance for me to
make my earthly advent!

11:34.736 --> 11:37.488
In order for me to
share this gift with you,

11:37.489 --> 11:40.366
we will first need
to form a pact.

11:40.367 --> 11:41.200
A pact?

11:41.201 --> 11:43.620
It's a whole thing.
Now, give me your hand.

11:45.455 --> 11:46.582
Now, then...

11:48.166 --> 11:50.501
This fight isn't over yet!

11:50.502 --> 11:54.088
What a perfect chance
for me to visit the surface.

11:54.089 --> 11:57.759
If I possess the child,
under the pretext of a pact...

11:58.051 --> 12:03.140
I'll be able to visit all my favorites
down there like Escher and Saria!

12:04.266 --> 12:05.767
So obvious...

12:06.018 --> 12:06.475
(Oink!!)

12:06.476 --> 12:11.023
Consider yourself lucky, child! I will
make good use of your body! (Oink!!)

12:18.530 --> 12:21.199
It's mine! The perfect body!

12:21.200 --> 12:23.534
It's the dawning
of the age of Jihriel!

12:23.535 --> 12:26.537
Wait, what the fudge?!

12:26.538 --> 12:28.998
You really screwed up
now, you dumbass angel!

12:28.999 --> 12:32.001
However much mana you expected
Prince Lloyd to have, he has way more!

12:32.002 --> 12:35.047
You only amount to a
palm's worth of his body!

12:35.964 --> 12:39.801
I'd wager this infernal creature
tried the same gambit, once...

12:40.260 --> 12:43.179
So, does that take
care of the pact?

12:43.180 --> 12:44.805
Oh... R-Right.

12:44.806 --> 12:47.183
In order to use divine sorcery,

12:47.184 --> 12:50.269
an angel must engrave the mana signature
upon the prospective caster's soul.

12:50.270 --> 12:53.814
After that, a pathway is
created by song, or other means.

12:53.815 --> 12:57.068
Is the whole singing thing
absolutely necessary...?

12:57.069 --> 13:02.698
Not in your case, child. Since I'm
with you, the path is already active.

13:02.699 --> 13:05.576
Simply call out with your soul.

13:05.577 --> 13:08.330
Call out with my soul...

13:18.841 --> 13:21.092
Prince Lloyd? Prince Lloyd!

13:21.093 --> 13:24.887
You okay, boss? You didn't catch
anything from that creep, did you?

13:24.888 --> 13:25.304
You little... You okay, boss? You didn't
catch anything from that creep, did you?

13:25.305 --> 13:26.514
I'm fine. I just had a vision of the
sorcerous language from before. You little...

13:26.515 --> 13:29.600
I'm fine. I just had a vision of the
sorcerous language from before.

13:29.601 --> 13:32.436
I understand it now intuitively,
now, instead of logically.

13:32.437 --> 13:35.607
I see. Divine sorcery
really is incredible.

13:35.774 --> 13:36.023
Hear that?! Incredible he says!

13:36.024 --> 13:38.234
This idiot might not realize what just
happened... Hear that?! Incredible he says!

13:38.235 --> 13:39.819
Stupid Grim! Porker Grim! This idiot
might not realize what just happened...

13:39.820 --> 13:40.903
but now that Prince Lloyd has mastered
divine sorcery, Stupid Grim! Porker Grim!

13:40.904 --> 13:43.740
but now that Prince Lloyd
has mastered divine sorcery,

13:43.991 --> 13:48.828
he's got enough power to conquer
both Paradise and the Netherworld!

13:48.829 --> 13:51.747
He could usurp the Demon
Lord's throne if he wanted!

13:51.748 --> 13:53.000
That said,

13:54.251 --> 13:59.005
I'm kind of disappointed.
Learning it was so easy...

13:59.006 --> 14:03.551
What are saying, child? Why
be disappointed to learn it easily?

14:03.552 --> 14:05.762
I enjoy the process, too.

14:06.305 --> 14:09.140
Instead of just
looking at the results...

14:09.141 --> 14:13.228
I enjoy exploring every
step of the construction.

14:14.021 --> 14:16.856
I've read spell books
until they fall apart,

14:16.857 --> 14:20.193
wondering, "Why's it like
this? Oh, is that why?!"

14:20.194 --> 14:22.279
Like I'm solving a riddle.

14:23.363 --> 14:26.741
And there are times,
when I've figured magic out,

14:26.742 --> 14:30.662
that it feels like I'm looking at the
face of the predecessors to created it all.

14:36.627 --> 14:42.299
Which is to say, y'know... I
don't mind the extra effort.

14:44.259 --> 14:46.802
A-Anyway, let's get to it!

14:46.803 --> 14:49.680
Your Luxa spell is
divine sorcery too, right?

14:49.681 --> 14:53.309
Right. It takes different
forms depending on the caster.

14:53.310 --> 14:55.812
For now, try conjuring a sword.

14:56.688 --> 15:02.569
I had wondered what brought him to Paradise
in pursuit of divine sorcery, but...

15:07.574 --> 15:10.535
Even through this thin
layer of skin, I can sense...

15:10.536 --> 15:13.580
the child's honest feelings.

15:14.081 --> 15:17.542
The kind of pure, genuine, sentiment
that you'd expect from an angel.

15:17.543 --> 15:20.838
Why, he reminds me of you...

15:21.213 --> 15:25.092
The one who earned
my respect, so long ago.

15:25.717 --> 15:30.304
Perhaps, in my service to
the gods, I had forgotten...

15:30.305 --> 15:37.104
I should follow the boy's example, and look
deeper, instead of only... the surface...

15:55.831 --> 15:57.582
(Wauuugh!)

15:57.583 --> 16:00.459
P-Prince Lloyd! Make it stop! Please! (Stupid! Stupid!
Enough! Enough! Prince Lloyd, you're terrifying!)

16:00.460 --> 16:02.670
How the hell is this that Luxa from before?! (Stupid!
Stupid! Enough! Enough! Prince Lloyd, you're terrifying!)

16:02.671 --> 16:04.338
That ain't no sword! (Stupid! Stupid! Enough!
Enough! Prince Lloyd, you're terrifying!)

16:04.339 --> 16:06.591
Aw, but I wasn't finished! (Stupid! Stupid!
Enough! Enough! Prince Lloyd, you're terrifying!)

16:06.592 --> 16:09.344
You're not?! That thing
is still under construction?!

16:09.469 --> 16:09.844
(Bwah!)

16:09.845 --> 16:11.053
Inconceivable. (Bwah!)

16:11.054 --> 16:11.762
Luxa's form can vary depending on the nature
and quantity of the caster's mana... (Bwah!)

16:11.763 --> 16:12.388
Luxa's form can vary depending on the
nature and quantity of the caster's mana...

16:12.389 --> 16:13.764
(Bwah!) Luxa's form can vary depending on the
nature and quantity of the caster's mana...

16:13.765 --> 16:14.182
Luxa's form can vary depending on the
nature and quantity of the caster's mana...

16:14.183 --> 16:15.099
(Bwah!) Luxa's form can vary depending on the
nature and quantity of the caster's mana...

16:15.100 --> 16:17.268
But for it to look
like this?! (Bwah!)

16:17.269 --> 16:17.311
(Bwah!)

16:18.145 --> 16:22.398
Now that I get a good look, it resembles
the shining eight wings of an archangel!

16:22.399 --> 16:25.860
That's way more than
eight! Archangel my ass!

16:25.861 --> 16:28.404
You need to get a
grip, you stupid angel!

16:28.405 --> 16:29.655
This is like a
divine revelation!

16:29.656 --> 16:34.660
Child—no, Prince Lloyd, I ask that
you allow me to accompany you!

16:34.661 --> 16:35.703
Shut up! Buzz off!

16:35.704 --> 16:40.501
Actually, do something about this
god of destruction-looking craziness!

16:43.045 --> 16:45.881
(I Was Reincarnated as the 7th Prince so I Can Take
My Time Perfecting My Magical Ability 2nd Season)

16:51.720 --> 16:57.017
You can still hear their performance
from inside the church out here.

17:01.063 --> 17:02.898
That thunder's got no manners.

17:04.399 --> 17:09.154
And then there's this smell...
that stands out in a church.

17:09.655 --> 17:14.158
The flowers are doing a decent job of
covering it up, but rats have sharp noses.

17:14.159 --> 17:18.079
I normally don't make a
point of digging around,

17:18.080 --> 17:22.292
but if this provides a clue to the
divine sorcery Prince Lloyd's is seeking...

17:23.585 --> 17:25.170
Are you lost, my friend?

17:26.255 --> 17:28.673
It's a big church, after all.

17:28.674 --> 17:31.677
Allow me to escort
you back to the recital.

17:32.386 --> 17:35.472
Right this way, if you will.

17:38.934 --> 17:41.769
No, I actually just love roses.

17:41.770 --> 17:43.688
I hope you don't mind
me looking around.

17:43.689 --> 17:45.857
That seems like such a waste.

17:45.858 --> 17:49.735
You came to see them
perform, didn't you?

17:49.736 --> 17:51.696
What about you?

17:51.697 --> 17:53.698
Well, I'm a pastor.

17:53.699 --> 17:58.244
And it's my duty to guide
parishioners who have gone astray.

17:58.245 --> 17:59.954
So you just
direct lost traffic?!

17:59.955 --> 18:03.457
That being said, despite
my many years of service,

18:03.458 --> 18:05.668
I still got lost
myself at times.

18:05.669 --> 18:07.378
Sounds like you
need a different duty!

18:07.379 --> 18:08.964
And you're supposed
to guide people?

18:10.299 --> 18:14.469
So... is that clumsiness of yours
why you're not wearing a Rosary?

18:15.137 --> 18:18.098
I was told that clergy need
to wear them at all times.

18:18.807 --> 18:21.476
I'm a total newcomer
and still received one.

18:21.935 --> 18:24.730
How... careless of me.

18:26.648 --> 18:29.735
But you're correct—a
blunder on my part.

18:31.236 --> 18:36.909
I know it's wrong... but I
always seem to forget it.

18:37.659 --> 18:39.243
Learn from my example.

18:39.244 --> 18:42.956
If you've joined the clergy,
you mustn't break such taboos.

18:43.248 --> 18:47.376
This garden is a holy place, as well,
where one should not tread lightly.

18:47.377 --> 18:48.754
My apologies.

18:49.046 --> 18:50.631
I'm new here, after all.

18:52.508 --> 18:56.636
There he is. Hey,
Babylon, what's wrong?

18:56.637 --> 18:58.514
The recital's gonna end soon.

19:03.018 --> 19:04.269
Shiro?

19:04.645 --> 19:09.024
I gotta say, you
seem rather devout.

19:09.942 --> 19:15.280
You must polish that thing every day...
either that, or you hardly ever wear it.

19:15.864 --> 19:20.160
Your Rosary seems a bit too pristine for such
a long withstanding member of the Church.

19:20.827 --> 19:22.996
Well, certainly.

19:23.705 --> 19:24.872
Shiro?

19:24.873 --> 19:28.126
Your furry friend has
quite the lovely coat.

19:29.837 --> 19:34.550
He must be well-taken care
of... Such a clever little dog.

19:39.137 --> 19:42.598
What're you guys doing out here?
What happened with the recital?

19:42.599 --> 19:45.644
I should ask you that! Where
did you run off to, Lloyd?

20:05.664 --> 20:09.417
Aw, what is it? What's got
you so affectionate, Shiro?

20:09.418 --> 20:11.003
Did you miss me?

20:13.213 --> 20:15.048
Souvenir attack!

20:19.011 --> 20:20.679
It can't be...

20:23.557 --> 20:24.766
Lloyd!

20:25.309 --> 20:26.517
How did you like the recital?

20:26.518 --> 20:27.519
Are you all right, miss?
How did you like the recital?

20:27.769 --> 20:29.938
We did our best!

20:31.023 --> 20:34.109
Yeah! It was an incredible
performance from start to finish!

20:35.277 --> 20:38.030
Actually, it was called off
because of the thunder...

20:40.532 --> 20:43.242
I've been waiting
for this day so long!

20:43.243 --> 20:45.537
I need to let them know how I—

20:45.996 --> 20:49.207
Right! It was an
incredible call to call it off!

20:49.208 --> 20:51.959
Sister Escher, I was wondering,

20:51.960 --> 20:54.504
is the inner garden
considered a sacred location?

20:54.505 --> 20:56.506
Just Escher is fine.

20:56.507 --> 21:02.136
And yes, we often use it to
lay pets of the faithful to rest.

21:02.137 --> 21:04.765
Is that where the smell
of rot was coming from...?

21:06.767 --> 21:09.268
It's hard to leave the
assassin life behind.

21:09.269 --> 21:12.564
I keep coming to
the worst conclusions.

21:13.524 --> 21:15.608
I guess it's fine since the
recital ended without incident,

21:15.609 --> 21:15.942
and Prince Lloyd doesn't
seem worried about it...

21:15.943 --> 21:17.818
Something wrong, Babylon? and Prince
Lloyd doesn't seem worried about it...

21:17.819 --> 21:18.529
and Prince Lloyd doesn't
seem worried about it...

21:18.779 --> 21:20.072
And yet...

21:21.031 --> 21:24.159
By the way, I'm leaving
the Church as of today.

21:25.619 --> 21:28.914
He seems to have found what
he needed, wherever he was,

21:29.289 --> 21:33.543
so the job's done. Whatever
happens to this church isn't my concern.

21:33.544 --> 21:36.296
Oh, right! Mr. Babylon,

21:36.547 --> 21:39.757
I still hadn't thanked you
for saving me this afternoon.

21:39.758 --> 21:42.010
I'm really grateful!

21:48.517 --> 21:51.060
It needed to be dirtier.

21:51.061 --> 21:53.938
Considering I had
lost my original Rosary,

21:53.939 --> 21:57.067
and only recently
received this new one.

22:01.113 --> 22:04.992
There's no need to
pursue them, but, yes...

22:05.659 --> 22:08.495
Let's increase
security around here.

22:09.580 --> 22:12.040
I don't need any interruptions.

22:14.334 --> 22:18.881
Not when the day is at hand.

23:50.556 --> 23:53.641
Pancakes. Pancakes are music.

23:53.642 --> 23:57.646
The ensemble of honey, syrup, and rich
butter creates the most sublime melody.

23:58.272 --> 24:00.314
Next time, on Episode 15:

24:00.315 --> 24:01.649
"Ghoul Hunting."
(Episode 15 Ghoul Hunting)

24:01.650 --> 24:02.066
(Episode 15 Ghoul Hunting)

24:02.067 --> 24:04.735
You will witness the depths of
sorcery. (Episode 15 Ghoul Hunting)

24:04.736 --> 24:04.945
(Episode 15 Ghoul Hunting)
